							'Visible image found. Double clicking image.\n' +
							'Group: ' + imageGroup + '\n' +
							'Key: ' + imageKey + '\n' +
							'Path: ' + imagePath
						)

						WindowsImageKeywords.doubleClickImage(imagePath)
						Windows.delay(2)

						return true
					}
				} catch (Exception e) {
					KeywordUtil.logInfo(
						'Image not double clickable yet.\n' +
						'Group: ' + imageGroup + '\n' +
						'Key: ' + imageKey + '\n' +
						'Reason: ' + e.getMessage()
					)
				}
			}

			Windows.delay(1)
			elapsedSeconds = elapsedSeconds + 1
		}

		return false
	}

	@Keyword
	void clickImageInsideImageOrStop(String imageGroup, String parentImageKey, String childImageKey) {
		String parentImage = getImage(imageGroup, parentImageKey)
		String childImage = getImage(imageGroup, childImageKey)

		try {
			WindowsImageKeywords.clickImageInImage(parentImage, childImage)
			Windows.delay(1)

			KeywordUtil.logInfo(
				'Clicked image inside image.\n' +
				'Group: ' + imageGroup + '\n' +
				'Parent image: ' + parentImageKey + '\n' +
				'Child image: ' + childImageKey
			)
		} catch (Exception e) {
			takeEvidence('ImageInsideImageClickFailed_' + sanitizeFileName(imageGroup + '_' + parentImageKey + '_' + childImageKey) + '.png')

			KeywordUtil.markFailedAndStop(
				'Could not click image inside image.\n' +
				'Group: ' + imageGroup + '\n' +
				'Parent image: ' + parentImageKey + '\n' +
				'Child image: ' + childImageKey + '\n' +
				'Parent path: ' + parentImage + '\n' +
				'Child path: ' + childImage + '\n' +
				'Reason: ' + e.getMessage()
			)
		}
	}

	@Keyword
	void takeEvidence(String fileName) {
		try {
			String evidenceDir = RunConfiguration.getReportFolder() + '\\Evidences\\'
			new File(evidenceDir).mkdirs()

			WindowsActionHelper
				.create(WindowsDriverFactory.getWindowsSession())
				.takeScreenshot(evidenceDir + fileName)

			KeywordUtil.logInfo('Evidence captured: ' + evidenceDir + fileName)
		} catch (Exception e) {
			KeywordUtil.logInfo('Could not capture evidence: ' + e.getMessage())
		}
	}

	private File resolveImageFileOrStop(String imageGroup, String imageKey, String relativePath) {
		File imageFile = resolveImageFile(relativePath)

		if (imageFile != null && imageFile.exists() && imageFile.isFile()) {
			KeywordUtil.logInfo(
				'Image file resolved.\n' +
				'Group: ' + imageGroup + '\n' +
				'Key: ' + imageKey + '\n' +
				'Path: ' + imageFile.getAbsolutePath()
			)

			return imageFile
		}

		File expectedFile = new File(
			RunConfiguration.getProjectDir(),
			normalizeRelativePath(relativePath)
		)

		KeywordUtil.markFailedAndStop(
			'Image file not resolved from project folder.\n' +
			'Group: ' + imageGroup + '\n' +
			'Key: ' + imageKey + '\n' +
			'Expected relative path: ' + relativePath + '\n' +
			'Expected absolute path: ' + expectedFile.getAbsolutePath() + '\n' +
			'Project dir: ' + RunConfiguration.getProjectDir() + '\n' +
			'Files in expected folder:\n' + listFilesInExpectedFolder(expectedFile) + '\n' +
			'Recursive matches inside Images:\n' + listRecursiveMatches(expectedFile.getName())
		)

		return null
	}

	private File resolveImageFile(String relativePath) {
		String normalizedRelativePath = normalizeRelativePath(relativePath)

		File exactFile = new File(
			RunConfiguration.getProjectDir(),
			normalizedRelativePath
		)

		if (exactFile.exists() && exactFile.isFile()) {
			return exactFile
		}

		File expectedFolder = exactFile.getParentFile()
		File fileFromExpectedFolder = findFileByNormalizedName(expectedFolder, exactFile.getName())

		if (fileFromExpectedFolder != null) {
			return fileFromExpectedFolder
		}

		File imagesFolder = new File(RunConfiguration.getProjectDir(), 'Images')
		File fileFromImagesFolder = findFileByNormalizedNameRecursive(imagesFolder, exactFile.getName())

		if (fileFromImagesFolder != null) {
			return fileFromImagesFolder
		}

		return null
	}

	private File findFileByNormalizedName(File folder, String expectedFileName) {
		if (folder == null || !folder.exists() || !folder.isDirectory()) {
			return null
		}

		String expectedName = normalizeFileName(expectedFileName)
		File[] files = folder.listFiles()

		if (files == null) {
			return null
		}

		for (File file : files) {
			if (file.isFile() && normalizeFileName(file.getName()).equals(expectedName)) {
				return file
			}
		}

		return null
	}

	private File findFileByNormalizedNameRecursive(File folder, String expectedFileName) {
		if (folder == null || !folder.exists() || !folder.isDirectory()) {
			return null
		}

		String expectedName = normalizeFileName(expectedFileName)
		File[] files = folder.listFiles()

		if (files == null) {
			return null
		}

		for (File file : files) {
			if (file.isFile() && normalizeFileName(file.getName()).equals(expectedName)) {
				return file
			}

			if (file.isDirectory()) {
				File found = findFileByNormalizedNameRecursive(file, expectedFileName)

				if (found != null) {
					return found
				}
			}
		}

		return null
	}

	private String listFilesInExpectedFolder(File expectedFile) {
		try {
			File folder = expectedFile.getParentFile()

			if (folder == null || !folder.exists()) {
				return 'Folder not found: ' + folder
			}

			File[] files = folder.listFiles()

			if (files == null || files.length == 0) {
				return 'Folder is empty: ' + folder.getAbsolutePath()
			}

			return files.collect { File file ->
				return file.getName() + ' -> ' + file.getAbsolutePath()
			}.sort().join('\n')
		} catch (Exception e) {
			return 'Could not list folder. Reason: ' + e.getMessage()
		}
	}

	private String listRecursiveMatches(String expectedFileName) {
		try {
			List<String> matches = []
			File imagesFolder = new File(RunConfiguration.getProjectDir(), 'Images')

			collectMatches(imagesFolder, normalizeFileName(expectedFileName), matches)

			if (matches.isEmpty()) {
				return 'No recursive match found.'
			}

			return matches.join('\n')
		} catch (Exception e) {
			return 'Could not search recursively. Reason: ' + e.getMessage()
		}
	}

	private void collectMatches(File folder, String expectedName, List<String> matches) {
		if (folder == null || !folder.exists() || !folder.isDirectory()) {
			return
		}

		File[] files = folder.listFiles()

		if (files == null) {
			return
		}

		for (File file : files) {
			if (file.isFile() && normalizeFileName(file.getName()).equals(expectedName)) {
				matches.add(file.getAbsolutePath())
			}

			if (file.isDirectory()) {
				collectMatches(file, expectedName, matches)
			}
		}
	}

	private String normalizeRelativePath(String relativePath) {
		return relativePath
			.replace('/', File.separator)
			.replace('\\', File.separator)
			.trim()
	}

	private String normalizeFileName(String name) {
		String normalized = Normalizer
			.normalize(name, Normalizer.Form.NFD)
			.replaceAll('\\p{InCombiningDiacriticalMarks}+', '')

		return normalized
			.toLowerCase()
			.replace('dimensions', 'dimension')
			.replaceAll('[^a-z0-9]', '')
	}

	private String sanitizeFileName(String value) {
		return value.replaceAll('[^a-zA-Z0-9_\\-]', '_')
	}

	private int getSafeTimeout(int timeoutSeconds) {
		if (timeoutSeconds <= 0) {
			return 1
		}

		return timeoutSeconds
	}

	private boolean isImageFound(def imageResult) {
		return imageResult != null && imageResult != false
	}

	private void validateGroup(String imageGroup) {
		if (imageGroup == null || imageGroup.trim().isEmpty()) {
			KeywordUtil.markFailedAndStop('Image group is empty.')
		}

		if (!IMAGE_GROUPS.containsKey(imageGroup)) {
			KeywordUtil.markFailedAndStop(
				'Image group not found: ' + imageGroup + '\n' +
				'Available groups: ' + IMAGE_GROUPS.keySet()
			)
		}
	}

	private void validateImageKey(String imageGroup, String imageKey) {
		validateGroup(imageGroup)

		if (imageKey == null || imageKey.trim().isEmpty()) {
			KeywordUtil.markFailedAndStop(
				'Image key is empty.\n' +
				'Group: ' + imageGroup
			)
		}

		if (!IMAGE_GROUPS[imageGroup].containsKey(imageKey)) {
			KeywordUtil.markFailedAndStop(
				'Image key not found: ' + imageKey + '\n' +
				'Group: ' + imageGroup + '\n' +
				'Available keys: ' + IMAGE_GROUPS[imageGroup].keySet()
			)
		}
	}
